{
  "info": {
    "name": "HerHealthGPT backend",
    "description": "Manual API testing for the HerHealthGPT backend.\n\nImport this collection and the `HerHealthGPT — local` environment, start the API with `make db-up && make migrate && make serve`, then send the requests. `baseUrl` comes from the environment so the same requests work against staging later.\n\nAs the Accounts endpoints land (register, verify, sign in, …) add them as folders here; the health check is the skeleton.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:8000",
      "type": "string"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Health",
      "description": "Liveness of the service and its database.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Health check",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/health",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["health"]
            },
            "description": "Returns 200 with {\"status\":\"ok\"} when the service can reach PostgreSQL, and 503 with {\"status\":\"unavailable\"} when it cannot. The check performs a real database round-trip, so a 503 means the database, not just the process, is the problem."
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is 200', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('body reports ok', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.json()).to.eql({ status: 'ok' });",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Registering",
      "description": "Issue #8: an email address and a password become an unverified user.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Register",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"woman@example.com\",\n  \"password\": \"correcthorse1\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/accounts/register",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["accounts", "register"]
            },
            "description": "Change the email between runs — the address is unique, so replaying this request as-is gets the 409 in the next request instead."
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is 201', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(201);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('response has no password field', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.json()).to.not.have.property('password');",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('new user is unverified', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.json().email_verified).to.eql(false);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Register — duplicate address",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"woman@example.com\",\n  \"password\": \"correcthorse1\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/accounts/register",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["accounts", "register"]
            },
            "description": "Run Register once first with this same address, then run this. Refused without revealing anything about the existing user."
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is 409', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(409);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Register — weak password",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"someone-else@example.com\",\n  \"password\": \"short\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/accounts/register",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["accounts", "register"]
            },
            "description": "Below the 8-character floor. The response names what is wrong with it."
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is 422', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(422);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('response names a reason', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.json().detail.reasons.length).to.be.above(0);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Signing in",
      "description": "Issue #9: sign in, stay signed in, sign out. Run Register (in the folder above) with an address first — Sign in needs a real user to authenticate against. Postman's cookie jar carries the access_token/refresh_token cookies these requests set automatically to later requests on the same domain, so run the requests below in order.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Sign in",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"woman@example.com\",\n  \"password\": \"correcthorse1\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/accounts/sign-in",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["accounts", "sign-in"]
            },
            "description": "Needs a user already registered with this address/password. Sets access_token (path /) and refresh_token (path /accounts) cookies, both httpOnly + secure + SameSite=Lax."
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is 200', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('access_token cookie is set', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.cookies.has('access_token')).to.be.true;",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('refresh_token cookie is set', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.cookies.has('refresh_token')).to.be.true;",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Sign in — wrong password",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"woman@example.com\",\n  \"password\": \"the-wrong-password\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/accounts/sign-in",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["accounts", "sign-in"]
            },
            "description": "A registered address with the wrong password. Compare the body against 'Sign in — unknown address' below — they must read identically."
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is 401', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(401);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Sign in — unknown address",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"nobody-registered@example.com\",\n  \"password\": \"whatever-password\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/accounts/sign-in",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["accounts", "sign-in"]
            },
            "description": "An address nobody registered. The response must be identical to 'Sign in — wrong password' — neither may reveal whether an address exists."
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is 401', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(401);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('body matches the wrong-password response', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.json()).to.eql({ detail: 'Incorrect email address or password.' });",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Me (signed in)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/accounts/me",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["accounts", "me"]
            },
            "description": "Run 'Sign in' first. Identifies the signed-in user from the access_token cookie alone — no body, no Authorization header."
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is 200', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('identifies the signed-in user', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.json().email).to.eql('woman@example.com');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Refresh",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/accounts/refresh",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["accounts", "refresh"]
            },
            "description": "Run 'Sign in' first. Exchanges the refresh_token cookie for a new access_token cookie — no body needed, the refresh_token cookie does the work."
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is 204', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(204);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('a new access_token cookie is set', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.cookies.has('access_token')).to.be.true;",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Sign out",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/accounts/sign-out",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["accounts", "sign-out"]
            },
            "description": "Run 'Sign in' first. Ends this one session — 'Me — after sign-out' below should then fail, since sign-out clears the cookies Postman is holding."
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is 204', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(204);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Me — after sign-out (expect 401)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/accounts/me",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["accounts", "me"]
            },
            "description": "Run 'Sign out' first. Proves sign-out actually ended the session rather than just clearing the client's cookies."
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is 401', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(401);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Sign out everywhere",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/accounts/sign-out-everywhere",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["accounts", "sign-out-everywhere"]
            },
            "description": "Run 'Sign in' first. Revokes every session for this user, not just the current one — to see the difference from plain 'Sign out', sign in from a second Postman cookie jar (or a private/incognito browser tab hitting the same API) and confirm its refresh token stops working too after this request."
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is 204', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(204);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Verifying",
      "description": "Issue #10: a code reaches her inbox, she types it in, her address is verified. Registering (in the folder above) already sends the first code — there is no `ConsoleEmailSender` HTTP endpoint, so read the code from the terminal running `make serve`: a line like `verification code for woman@example.com: 123456`. Paste that digit string into the requests below.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Verify email — correct code",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"woman@example.com\",\n  \"code\": \"PASTE_THE_CODE_FROM_THE_SERVER_CONSOLE\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/accounts/verify-email",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["accounts", "verify-email"]
            },
            "description": "Run Register with this address first, then replace the code with the 6-digit one logged to the server's console."
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is 200', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('address is now verified', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.json().email_verified).to.eql(true);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Verify email — wrong code",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"woman@example.com\",\n  \"code\": \"000000\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/accounts/verify-email",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["accounts", "verify-email"]
            },
            "description": "A code that is (almost certainly) not the real one. Counts as one of MAX_ATTEMPTS wrong guesses against whatever code is currently live for this address."
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is 400', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(400);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('reads as incorrect, not expired', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.json().detail).to.eql('That code is incorrect.');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Verify email — already used (expect expired)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"woman@example.com\",\n  \"code\": \"PASTE_THE_CODE_THAT_JUST_SUCCEEDED\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/accounts/verify-email",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["accounts", "verify-email"]
            },
            "description": "Run 'Verify email — correct code' first, then replay the same code. A code is single-use — this must read as expired, not as a second success and not as merely incorrect."
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is 400', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(400);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('reads as expired, not incorrect', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.json().detail).to.eql('This code has expired. Request a new one.');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Resend verification code",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"woman@example.com\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/accounts/verify-email/resend",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["accounts", "verify-email", "resend"]
            },
            "description": "Issues a fresh code, superseding whatever code this address had — check the server console for the new one. Does nothing (but still returns 204) if the address is unregistered or already verified, and does not say which."
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is 204', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(204);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Resend verification code — unknown address",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"nobody-registered@example.com\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/accounts/verify-email/resend",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["accounts", "verify-email", "resend"]
            },
            "description": "An address nobody registered. Must return the same 204 as a real address — nothing is actually sent, but the response cannot say so, or it would confirm the address is unregistered."
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is 204', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(204);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('body is empty either way', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.text()).to.eql('');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
